            <div xml:id="d640">

                <pb facs="0537" n="525" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg525"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/26601: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé at Tangier</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Childs</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tangier</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-12-17T23:00:00+01:00">December 17,
                            1942—11 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received December 18—10:40 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>849. The following telegram has been sent to Algiers.</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>96, December 17, 11 p.m. For Murphy. In accordance with Department’s telegram
                        number 267, December 14, 11 [<hi rendition="#italic">10</hi>] p.m. I saw
                        General Orgaz today and stated that General Patton desired to pay him a
                        visit of courtesy. I explained that General Eisenhower would have liked to
                        call on him but he would doubtless appreciate that it was difficult for
                        General Eisenhower to absent himself at this time but he hoped to give
                        himself the pleasure of calling on Orgaz at an early date.</p>
                    <p>Orgaz said he was leaving for Madrid on the 19th but would return about 23d
                        after which date he would be pleased to receive General Patton. I said that
                        I would be at Orgaz’ disposition upon his return in order to make whatever
                        arrangements might be necessary.</p>
                    <p>It is possible Orgaz may wish to offer a luncheon to General Patton. If he
                        does not, I shall be pleased to arrange such a luncheon at the Legation to
                        which Orgaz would be invited if this is agreeable. Repeated to Madrid and to
                        Department as my number 849. Childs.</p>
                </quote>
                <pb facs="0538" n="526" xml:id="pg526"/>
                <p>I mentioned to Orgaz before leaving that Ambassador Hayes desires to meet him.
                    Orgaz stated he had hoped to call on him on his last visit but he had too little
                    time.</p>
                <p>If it were possible on this occasion, he would do so but he was not certain.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Childs</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
